2.4 Handoff sequence

Use a compact S-A-F-E script for each resident:

Status/change: identity, new admission/return, baseline change, immediate concern.

Assistance: diet/liquid, transfer/ambulation, toileting, ADL and communication needs.

Focus tasks: time-critical care completed and still due.

Escalation: what was reported, to whom/when, what the incoming CNA must watch for.

Echo/read-back: incoming CNA repeats high-risk transfer, diet, isolation, and outstanding-task items.

This is compatible with AHRQ's structured handoff approach and can be mapped to SBAR or I-PASS if the facility already uses those tools (AHRQ Handoff Tool; AHRQ I-PASS Tool).

